    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d520">

                <pb facs="0529" n="521" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg521"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.014C/115: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Costa
                        Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hornibrook</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-13T19:00:00-05:00">November 13,
                            1939—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>63. Your despatch no. 938, October 30, 1939.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d520-f1"/>
                    There has been no change in the position of this Government regarding the
                    possible purchase of Cocos Island, as stated in the Department’s instruction no.
                    34 of January 4, 1938.<anchor n="5" xml:id="d520-f2"/> If the question of
                    purchase of the Island is again raised with you or any member of the Legation,
                    you should be guided accordingly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
